# Two stations with a polynomial basis of degree 2,147,483,647: C(m + 2, 2) basis functions
# is about 2.3e18, far above what an int holds. fBNAlp must refuse it in one line
# (examples/check/check.sh). This input goes through the binomial loop of
# srbm_params_check_size(), whose product is checked before anything is read from it.

dimension   2
grid_n      12
basis_m     2147483647
grid_type   uniform
solver      highs

drift
  -1.0  -1.0

covariance
  1.0  0.0
  0.0  1.0

reflection_form  minus_only
reflection
  1.0  0.0
  0.0  1.0

upper_bounds
  10.0  10.0
